{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/51103-similarities-between-garou-and-the-pure","id":51103,"title":"Similarities between Garou and the Pure?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-16T15:20:36-08:00","id":51103,"title":"Similarities between Garou and the Pure?","content":"I have often read that there are many similarities between the Garou (From Apocalypse) and the Pure. Honestly, I personally can not see many similarities, perhaps among the tribes. (such as Ivory Claws and Silver Fangs) What similarities are there between the two groups?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1999-wolf","name":"Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T16:09:21-08:00","id":51134,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about Apocalypse, but I've heard about the same similarities. I believe they remark upon the Zealotry of the Fire-Touched, the obsession with lineage for the Ivory Claws, and the eschewing of the trappings of humanity and turning the world back to its natural state (Pangaea) of the Predator Kings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T20:01:03-08:00","id":51317,"title":"","content":"Well during the Time of Judgement books right after Apocalypse came out WW did a survey for which tribes they wanted to see in the new game. Silver Fangs = Ivory Claws. Red Talons = Predator Kings. I believe Children of Gaia became Fire Touched. So basically Forsaken is a more dark brutal version of Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T22:27:41-08:00","id":51402,"title":"","content":"There are no *intentional* similarities between the Pure and the werewolves from Apocalypse, according to Ethan Skemp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T05:26:36-08:00","id":51555,"title":"","content":"At Silver Fangs = Ivory Claws and Red Talons = Predator Kings I see the similarities, but Fire Touched = Children of Gaia? o_o For me, the Fire Touched are more the antithesis of the Children of Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1999-wolf","name":"Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T05:48:44-08:00","id":51563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/51103-similarities-between-garou-and-the-pure?p=51555#post51555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Silver Fangs = Ivory Claws and Red Talons = Predator Kings I see the similarities, but Fire Touched = Children of Gaia? o_o For me, the Fire Touched are more the antithesis of the Children of Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that was the way it was meant to be. Not a direct crossover per se but just the general ideas with a darker, cold, and more brutal twist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T05:50:03-08:00","id":51564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/51103-similarities-between-garou-and-the-pure?p=51402#post51402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no *intentional* similarities between the Pure and the werewolves from Apocalypse, according to Ethan Skemp.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea I just remember the poll that was around at the time. Then when you read the WtF core you notice the similarities between the tribes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T06:26:18-08:00","id":51576,"title":"","content":"Take the Garou and consider all the mistakes they've made during their history or the aspects of their culture they're usually criticized for, ignore all their positive aspects and what you get is really, really close to the Pure. And I say that as a firm believer that the good sides of the Gaurou outbalance the bad ones and, all their screw-ups notwithanding, they still have the potential to make amend and help the world.<br /> <br /> The zealotry, the unwavering rage, the belief of superiority, the complete refusal to find a common ground with others and cooperate, the utter disdain for humans: it's all there. It's not hard to guess that the Pure would have gladly endorsed the Impergium or the War of Rage.<br /> <br /> The Ivory Claws and Predator Kings similarities are a litte more straightforward. I mean, in Apocalypse, the Predator Kings were a camp famous for its viciousness, hatred for mankind (and among the Red Talons, that means you <i>really</i> hate mankind) and desire to return to a primal world, and the Ivory Claws are what happens when you take the obsessions for &quot;blood purity&quot; Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords and Fianna had, then mix it with the most...unfortunate beliefs of the extremist fringes of the Get of Fenris.<br /> <br /> The Fire Touched are more their own thing, I think, but they share the same fanaticism <i>all </i>the Garou tribes manifested regulary.<br /> <br /> Again, the Garou were not only this, but it's pretty easy to see that, if you strip the Garou Nation of its redeeeming qualities, there are indeed some similarities between the Garou and the Pure, intentional or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-19-2014, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T07:04:12-08:00","id":51594,"title":"","content":"The other way someone put it was the Pure are what the Garou Nation would probably look like from an outside observer perspective: anti-human, anti-tech, pro-spirit, racist/blood purist, overly-violent and very insular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T13:56:41-08:00","id":54881,"title":"","content":"To the one saying the fire touched are the anti thesis of the children of gaia, Rabid wolf was apparently originally something else, and according to spiritual lore rumor the death of father wolf drove him insane. Thought that warranted a note. <br /> <br /> Predator kings are all kinds of bad ass by the way. Alphas of alphas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T23:08:16-08:00","id":56596,"title":"","content":"The Predator Kings aren't alphas. They're terrible leaders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join 